turn it on all by himself?

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:52.070
- Maggie lays him down to
sleep, and when he awoke,

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:53.930
his life would be changed forever.

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:55.970
He's woken up by a man named Mike Norris,

00:02:55.970 --> 00:02:58.420
a homicide detective with the
Chicago Police Department,

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:00.230
who informs him that
Maggie had an accident

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:01.800
and starts asking him questions.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:03.830
His mom returns home
from work, very worried,

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:05.510
and she orders Andy to stay in his room.

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:07.610
He realizes that the tiny
footprints on the counter

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:10.040
near the scene of the accident
match Chucky's footprints,

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:11.577
but the adults obviously
don't believe him,

00:03:11.577 --> 00:03:12.700
and this opens him up

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:14.740
to be psychologically
manipulated by Chucky.

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:16.500
His mom thinks that he's
being a troublemaker

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:17.980
and telling stories, and again,

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:19.560
there's no father figure in his life.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:21.030
There's a natural tendency for a child

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:22.490
to attach themselves to an adult.

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:24.280
It's basically their survival instinct,

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:25.900
since they can't yet
take care of themselves.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:28.150
Karen Barclay is a struggling single mom,

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:29.830
she's exhausted, she can barely afford

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:30.750
to get care for her son

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:32.590
and she has to spend
a lot of time at work.

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:35.010
Psychology studies show
that lack of a father figure

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:37.270
can lead to low self-esteem
and misbehavior,

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:39.660
and Chucky essentially tries
to manipulate the situation

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:41.630
by inserting himself into the father role,

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:43.730
forcing Andy to attach himself to him.

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:45.950
Chucky tells him his real
name is Charles Lee Ray,

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:47.280
and that he'd been sent down from heaven

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:48.530
by his daddy to play with him.

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:50.570
He does this to try to
gain control over Andy,

00:03:50.570 --> 00:03:52.620
the way a father has
control over his child.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:54.120
Andy doesn't have the life experience

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.210
to know how this looks from
someone else's perspective,

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:57.820
and eventually just apologizes

00:03:57.820 --> 00:03:59.440
and promises to stop making up stories

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:00.360
to appease his mother.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:02.020
The next day he brings Chucky to school,

