until Norris is finally able to end it

00:09:01.550 --> 00:09:02.990
by shooting the doll through the heart.

00:09:02.990 --> 00:09:04.360
But a lot of damage is done,

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:06.670
because Andy witnessed all
of this horrendous stuff

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:07.750
up close and personal.

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:09.740
The whole ordeal represents an environment

00:09:09.740 --> 00:09:10.820
of domestic turmoil,

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:12.490
which the National Library of Medicine

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:15.180
cites can result in
Developmental Trauma Disorder.

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:16.870
A child's brain still spends a lot of time

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:19.540
developing after birth, and
it may react to these events,

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:20.960
causing abnormal behavior.

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:23.950
Some symptoms include hyper-vigilance
and inexplicable fear,

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:26.820
deep-seated shame and isolation
from making connections.

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:28.690
Dr. Arthur Becker-Weidman does a good job

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:30.050
of explaining this in an interview

00:09:30.050 --> 00:09:31.693
at NYU's Child Study Center.

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:37.080
- Their stress response
system is always activated,

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:41.510
and the stress response
system is focused on survival.

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:43.060
- We see this in the final shot

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:44.270
of the original Child's Play

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:46.030
as Andy stares at the severed head,

00:09:46.030 --> 00:09:48.470
perhaps unable to believe
that Chucky is really dead.

00:09:48.470 --> 00:09:49.990
He's not gonna let his guard down today,

00:09:49.990 --> 00:09:51.660
or during the years that would follow.

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:53.180
Andy had to testify in court.

00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:55.150
His mom backed up his
story, but the police,

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:56.530
for whatever reason, did not,

00:09:56.530 --> 00:09:58.450
causing Mrs. Barclay to look crazy

00:09:58.450 --> 00:09:59.690
and be sent to the loonie bin.

00:09:59.690 --> 00:10:01.520
The judge ordered
psychiatric care for Andy,

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:03.800
landing him in the Midtown
Children's Crisis Center.

00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:05.800
He's haunted by bad dreams of Chucky,

00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:08.080
but he doesn't wanna talk
about with his psychiatrist,

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:11.030
an example of his emotional
isolation caused by DTD.

00:10:11.030 --> 00:10:13.040
Instead of telling about his
bad dreams to the shrink,

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:15.520
he tells what actually happened in 1988.

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:19.050
It is October 1990 when Andy
is designated for foster care,

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:21.550
assuming this calendar is
accurate to real weekdays.

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:22.870
The Center tells the foster parents,

00:10:22.870 --> 00:10:23.990
Phil and Joanne Simpson,

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:25.010
that the stories about the doll

00:10:25.010 --> 00:10:27.830
were some kind of coping mechanism
for what really happened.

00:10:27.830 --> 00:10:29.300
- Well, in order to come to terms

00:10:29.300 --> 00:10:31.830
with something he couldn't
possibly understand,

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:34.130
he turned it all into
a kind of fairy tale.

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:36.970
He insisted his doll was responsible.

00:10:36.970 --> 00:10:40.550
Said it was possessed by
the soul of Charles Lee Ray.

00:10:40.550 --> 00:10:42.210
- On the way home,
they're nearly flattened

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:43.560
by a Good Guys truck.

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:45.270
The dolls and merchandise
are still popular,

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:47.340
and this makes it much
harder for Andy to recover,

00:10:47.340 --> 00:10:49.710
because he's constantly being
triggered into high alert.

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:51.670
After meeting his new foster sister, Kyle,

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:53.630
his PTSD is activated once again

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:55.660
when an old Good Guy doll
falls out of the closet.

00:10:55.660 --> 00:10:57.660
That night, Joanne reads
him a bedtime story,

00:10:57.660 --> 00:10:59.280
hoping to give him a sense of normalcy.

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:00.600
Andy really misses his mom

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:01.940
and doesn't wanna be left alone,

00:11:01.940 --> 00:11:03.790
because even now, nearly two years

00:11:03.790 --> 00:11:06.110
after his two days with
Chucky, he's paranoid.

00:11:06.110 --> 00:11:07.780
He asks Mrs. Simpson to sing him to sleep

00:11:07.780 --> 00:11:09.810
like his mother used
to, but as he dozes off,

00:11:09.810 --> 00:11:12.000
he's still alarmed by sounds in the night.

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:14.160
The next morning, he and
Kyle are both grounded

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:15.760
when this broken statue is discovered,

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:17.300
so Andy helps Kyle with the laundry

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:19.680
and takes a puff of her cigarette
while holding it for her.

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:21.900
She tries to explain that
cigarettes are bad for him,

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:23.530
and that only grown-ups
are allowed to do things

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:24.363
that are bad for them,

00:11:24.363 --> 00:11:26.750
which he counters by saying
that she's not a grown up,

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:28.040
which gets on her nerves.

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:29.480
I find the dynamic interesting

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:31.040
because smoking is often used

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:33.180
as an unhealthy coping
mechanism by adults,

00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:34.690
and Andy is getting involved with it

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:36.430
at a way too young of an age.

00:11:36.430 --> 00:11:39.090
But he's seen more agony
than a lot of adults have.

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:40.820
This may also have been a gateway for him,

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:42.970
because he's seen to be a
smoker later on in life.

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:44.820
It seems that Andy is also self-conscious

00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:47.200
about the burden that his
psychological issues present.

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:48.990
He overhears Mr. and Mrs. Simpson debating

00:11:48.990 --> 00:11:50.520
whether they're qualified
to take care of him,

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:52.650
which plays into the shame
and low self-esteem issues

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:54.430
connected to his psychological issues.

00:11:54.430 --> 00:11:55.660
He's also still paranoid.

00:11:55.660 --> 00:11:57.230
He sees the Good Guy
doll that Mrs. Simpson

00:11:57.230 --> 00:11:59.070
was supposed to have
gotten rid of downstairs,

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:01.503
and he's off put by this small hesitation.

00:12:02.481 --> 00:12:04.550
- Hi, I'm Tommy!

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:06.330
- Andy decides to check
the batteries to make sure

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:07.940
this wasn't a repeat situation.

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:10.250
That evening, he hangs out
with Kyle in the backyard.

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:12.550
I imagine it was good for
him to have a real friend.

00:12:12.550 --> 00:12:13.920
It goes back to the attachment theory

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:14.890
that I brought up earlier.

00:12:14.890 --> 00:12:16.610
He's not as comfortable
with his foster parents,

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:18.820
because he senses they feel
that they can't handle him,

00:12:18.820 --> 00:12:20.930
but Kyle's in the same
situation that he's in,

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:22.440
and they kind of bond over that.

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:24.430
The next night, Chucky
makes his move against Andy,

00:12:24.430 --> 00:12:26.230
by tying him up and
gagging him with a sock

00:12:26.230 --> 00:12:27.820
in order to perform the voodoo ritual

00:12:27.820 --> 00:12:28.980
and transfer his conscience

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:30.850
out of the doll's body and into his.

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:32.610
We've already established
that the kid's been dealing

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:33.680
with some nightmare issues.

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:34.620
It's not really something

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:36.060
that's explored again going forward,

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:37.890
but this is the third time
now that he's woken up

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:40.150
to some horrific circumstance
caused by Chucky.

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:42.430
I imagine that makes it
pretty hard to fall asleep.

00:12:42.430 --> 00:12:43.640
This time, he gets out of it,

00:12:43.640 --> 00:12:45.160
because Kyle had snuck out that night

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:46.790
and she was coming back
in through his window,

00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:48.250
forcing Chucky to go inanimate

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:50.310
so that nobody finds
out he's really alive.

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:52.600
This once again put
Andy in a bad position.

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:54.770
He doesn't have an explanation
for how he got tied up,

00:12:54.770 --> 00:12:56.350
so he's forced to tell the truth,

00:12:56.350 --> 00:12:57.840
which makes him look like a nut.

00:12:57.840 --> 00:12:59.680
Andy is still too young to understand

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:01.940
that the word of a 7-year-old
will never convince them,

00:13:01.940 --> 00:13:02.890
he needs proof.

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:05.300
Mr. Simpson is fed up with
all of Andy's Chucky stories,

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:06.880
and he locks the doll in the basement.

00:13:06.880 --> 00:13:09.150
The next day would be Andy's
first at his new school,

00:13:09.150 --> 00:13:10.780
where he would be pushed
to his breaking point

00:13:10.780 --> 00:13:12.930
and go on the offensive
for the first time.

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:24.000
In the morning, Kyle walks
Andy to the school bus,

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:26.010
and tries to give him some
advice for his first day,

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:27.470
telling him not to act nervous,

00:13:27.470 --> 00:13:29.890
because Andy's constantly
looking back for Chucky.

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:32.170
It's not just Chucky that he
has to worry about though,

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:35.903
there's also this INCREDIBLY
hostile kid on the bus.

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:44.250
I know I bring this up every time,

00:13:44.250 --> 00:13:45.770
and you're probably sick of seeing it now

00:13:45.770 --> 00:13:48.560
if you watch my channel, but I
just can't get over this kid.

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:50.913
What happened to him? Why is he like this?

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:54.080
But it's here that we
see the isolation aspect

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:55.980
of Andy's trauma fully on display.

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:58.500
He sits alone on the bus and
plays alone on the playground;

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:00.330
it looks like he's actually
just pretending to play

00:14:00.330 --> 00:14:01.940
so he can keep an eye out for Chucky.

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:03.960
At the end of the day,
Andy finds a Good Guy doll

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:06.190
hidden in a cabinet and gets
chewed out by the teacher

00:14:06.190 --> 00:14:07.920
for writing obscenities on his schoolwork,

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:10.820
which he obviously didn't
do, and ends up in detention.

00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:12.500
The teacher locks the doll in a closet,

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:14.130
and when Andy gets up to investigate

00:14:14.130 --> 00:14:17.780
and see if this was in
fact Chucky, he sees this.

00:14:17.780 --> 00:14:18.780
- [CHUCKY] Peek a boo!

00:14:18.780 --> 00:14:20.530
- [ZAC] He finds himself
locked in the classroom

00:14:20.530 --> 00:14:22.000
and has to use the window to escape,

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:24.110
but after explaining everything
to his foster parents,

00:14:24.110 --> 00:14:25.470
they remember the broken statue

00:14:25.470 --> 00:14:28.190
and view this as another
example of Andy acting out,

00:14:28.190 --> 00:14:29.180
which they had been warned about

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:30.650
by the center they fostered him from.

00:14:30.650 --> 00:14:32.150
Mr. Simpson takes him to the basement

00:14:32.150 --> 00:14:33.880
and shows him that the
doll is still lying there

00:14:33.880 --> 00:14:34.713
where he left it,

00:14:34.713 --> 00:14:36.500
but Andy knows what he
saw at school that day.

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:37.360
In the middle of the night,

00:14:37.360 --> 00:14:39.730
he wakes up and steals the
carving knife from the kitchen,

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:41.877
and bravely goes down to confront Chucky,

00:14:41.877 --> 00:14:44.280
but the Good Guy is no longer in his spot.

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:45.810
Chucky surprises him from above,

00:14:45.810 --> 00:14:47.630
but he's able to recover
in time to slice Chucky

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:49.330
in the head, causing the doll to retreat.

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:51.300
However, the noise wakes up Mr. Simpson,

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:53.230
and Chucky silently grabs a fire poker

00:14:53.230 --> 00:14:54.370
to trip him on the stairs.

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:57.110
He's left hanging upside down,
and when Chucky releases him,

00:14:57.110 --> 00:14:58.610
the impact breaks his neck,

00:14:58.610 --> 00:15:01.000
tallying up another victim
for Charles Lee Ray.

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:02.890
Mrs. Simpson was always the more patient

00:15:02.890 --> 00:15:04.020
of the two foster parents,

00:15:04.020 --> 00:15:06.230
often standing up for Andy
against Phil's concerns

00:15:06.230 --> 00:15:07.063
about his psyche,

00:15:07.063 --> 00:15:08.910
but the loss of her husband from something

00:15:08.910 --> 00:15:10.480
that she perceives to be Andy's fault,

00:15:10.480 --> 00:15:12.060
ends up being her last straw.

00:15:12.060 --> 00:15:14.300
Before being shipped back to
the Children's Crisis Center,

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:15.530
Andy tries to warn Kyle

00:15:15.530 --> 00:15:17.520
that Chucky is still down in the cellar.

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:19.030
- Don't let him get you too.

00:15:19.030 --> 00:15:21.470
- The woman at the Crisis
Center, Grace, puts Andy to bed,

00:15:21.470 --> 00:15:23.410
but as soon as she leaves
the room, he's back up,

00:15:23.410 --> 00:15:24.660
getting changed out of his pajamas

00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:26.650
and into some warmer
clothes and running shoes.

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:28.900
Compared to Chucky's
first incarnation in '88,

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:30.750
Andy's already being more proactive

00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:32.270
and not just letting himself be the victim

00:15:32.270 --> 00:15:33.560
of what happens to him anymore.

00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:34.760
By the time Chucky arrives,

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:36.700
Andy is basically already waiting for him.

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:38.440
We can see how he's matured in this way,

00:15:38.440 --> 00:15:40.800
he's given up on trying to
convince the adults to help him,

00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:42.290
and he's just gonna do whatever he can

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:43.730
to protect himself on his own.

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:46.160
He probably picked this up from Kyle.

00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:50.250
- Every time it happens,
it just makes me stronger,

00:15:50.250 --> 00:15:52.000
because it reminds me that the only one

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:53.760
I can count on is myself.

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:55.840
- The fire alarm goes off
in the middle of the night,

00:15:55.840 --> 00:15:57.790
and Andy spots Chucky at
the bottom of the stairs

00:15:57.790 --> 00:15:58.770
in Kyle's arms.

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:01.240
Grace thinks that Kyle, one
of her former troublemakers,

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:02.410
was the one to pull the alarm,

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:03.960
and pulls them both into her office,

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:05.730
where she's stabbed in
the heart by Chucky.

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:07.725
- [CHUCKY] Snap out of it,

00:16:07.725 --> 00:16:10.560
you act like you've never
seen a dead body before!

00:16:10.560 --> 00:16:13.170
- I mean, he... he has a point.

00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:14.840
I mean, Andy should be
used to this by now.

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:17.240
With Andy at knifepoint, they
sneak away from the center

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:18.990
and get into the back
of a newspaper truck,

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:20.060
where Chucky tries to perform

00:16:20.060 --> 00:16:21.500
the soul transfer ritual again,

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:23.300
but is again interrupted by Kyle,

00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:24.520
who cuts off the truck driver,

00:16:24.520 --> 00:16:26.460
forcing Andy and Chucky to flee on foot.

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:28.730
Kyle chases them back
to the Play Pal factory

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:30.500
where the Good Guy dolls are manufactured,

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:33.090
where Chucky frantically finds
a spot to perform his ritual,

00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:35.580
but this time discovers
that he's too late.

00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:36.770
From his incarnation,

00:16:36.770 --> 00:16:38.540
Chucky only has a limited amount of time

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:41.000
to transfer his soul out of
his body before turning human,

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:43.160
and being stuck in the
Good Guy doll until death.

00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:44.560
With possession out of the picture,

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:46.690
his consolation plan is revenge.

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:48.960
You know, if you can't join 'em, kill 'em.

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:51.630
Luckily for Andy, Kyle knocks
over a wall of Good Guy boxes

00:16:51.630 --> 00:16:53.210
and takes his hand to help him flee.

00:16:53.210 --> 00:16:55.210
A long chase through the
factory's assembly line

00:16:55.210 --> 00:16:56.430
culminates when Andy opens

00:16:56.430 --> 00:16:58.340
this scalding hot plastic overflow valve

00:16:58.340 --> 00:17:00.400
and rushes to save Kyle
from the heat press.

00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:01.940
It's interesting to see how he's always

00:17:01.940 --> 00:17:03.520
the one to attack Chucky with heat,

00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:05.220
and this wouldn't be the last time either.

00:17:05.220 --> 00:17:07.570
Eventually, it's Kyle who
grabs a loose air hose

00:17:07.570 --> 00:17:09.210
and forces it into Chucky's mouth.

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:10.900
The hot plastic dries around the hose,

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:14.020
causing Chucky's head to blow
up like a balloon and explode.

00:17:14.020 --> 00:17:15.559
Like Eddie Caputo's house.

00:17:15.559 --> 00:17:16.392
*EXPLOSION AND SPLATTER*

00:17:17.850 --> 00:17:20.550
The sun rises as they
walk out of the factory.

00:17:20.550 --> 00:17:22.093
- [Andy] Where are we going?
- [Kyle] Home.

00:17:23.870 --> 00:17:24.970
- [Andy] Where's home?

00:17:25.806 --> 00:17:27.920
- [Kyle] Andy, I have no idea.

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:30.360
- And neither do I,
because we don't see Andy

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:31.880
for another nine years.

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:34.570
According to this file,
Andy is now 16 years old.

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:36.750
If Andy turned six in November 1988,

00:17:36.750 --> 00:17:39.350
he would turn 16 in November of 1998.

00:17:39.350 --> 00:17:41.290
It looks like there's snow on
the ground, but it's melting,

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:43.310
so I'm gonna go with spring 1999

00:17:43.310 --> 00:17:44.580
as the next time we see him.

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:46.410
Andy is put into Kent Military School

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:48.500
for delinquent activities
prompting probation

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:50.470
and juvenile authorities jurisdiction.

00:17:50.470 --> 00:17:52.670
We've never really seen
Andy to be a bad kid,

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:54.950
but since most rational
people were of the belief

00:17:54.950 --> 00:17:56.240
that Chucky was never alive,

00:17:56.240 --> 00:17:57.430
it's easy to blame Andy

00:17:57.430 --> 00:17:59.180
for a lot of those things that happened.

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:00.830
However, it's likely that he did

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:02.900
get into some actual
trouble in his pre-teen

00:18:02.900 --> 00:18:03.970
and early teen years,

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:06.560
and it's not hard to imagine
that with no parental guidance,

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:07.410
he could have found himself

00:18:07.410 --> 00:18:09.170
on the wrong side of the law a few times.

00:18:09.170 --> 00:18:12.800
Since Chucky never comes
back between 1991 and 1999,

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:14.180
it looks like Andy did kind of

00:18:14.180 --> 00:18:15.840
turn into a delinquent on his own.

00:18:15.840 --> 00:18:18.600
So we have to assume that he
was not a well-disciplined kid

00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:20.900
and he finds himself in
military school because of it.

00:18:20.900 --> 00:18:22.070
When the Colonel reads his file,

00:18:22.070 --> 00:18:23.600
he tells him that he'll have to behave.

00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:25.460
No more fantasies of killer dolls.

00:18:25.460 --> 00:18:26.350
While getting his haircut,

00:18:26.350 --> 00:18:28.730
Andy discovers that the Good
Guy doll is back on the market

00:18:28.730 --> 00:18:31.110
after being pulled in the
aftermath of bad publicity

00:18:31.110 --> 00:18:33.280
and lawsuits from what
transpired at the factory.

00:18:33.280 --> 00:18:35.220
That evening, he discovers
his new roommate,

00:18:35.220 --> 00:18:37.080
Harold Whitehurst has
been locked in the closet

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:38.470
by cadet Lieutenant Shelton.

00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:39.350
It's hard to say for sure

00:18:39.350 --> 00:18:40.780
what was going through Andy's head here,

00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:43.350
but it looks as if he's still
getting flashbacks of Chucky,

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:45.760
because the way he approaches
the closet is very similar

00:18:45.760 --> 00:18:48.260
to when Chucky was locked in
the closet at Andy's school.

00:18:48.260 --> 00:18:49.330
During drill formations,

00:18:49.330 --> 00:18:51.050
Shelton picks on Andy because he's new,

00:18:51.050 --> 00:18:52.950
but one other cadet stands up for him,

00:18:52.950 --> 00:18:55.423
which leads to Andy finding a new flame.

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:06.170
Andy takes a liking to a female cadet

00:19:06.170 --> 00:19:07.290
named Kristen De Silva.

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:08.590
There are obviously a lot of theories

00:19:08.590 --> 00:19:09.790
about dating compatibility,

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:11.350
but it looks like what
they're going for here

00:19:11.350 --> 00:19:12.910
is the opposites attract theory.

00:19:12.910 --> 00:19:15.670
De Silva is fearless, standing
up to her superior officer,

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:17.350
outperforming her class
at the shooting range

00:19:17.350 --> 00:19:19.100
and sneaking around the halls at night.

00:19:19.100 --> 00:19:21.090
Andy is traumatized by a children's toy,

00:19:21.090 --> 00:19:23.160
can't hit a target and
is basically a runner,

00:19:23.160 --> 00:19:25.240
he doesn't seem to stay
in one place too long.

00:19:25.240 --> 00:19:26.220
The idea behind this theory

00:19:26.220 --> 00:19:28.130
is that we as humans look for a partner

00:19:28.130 --> 00:19:29.730
who fills in the traits that we lack,

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:31.860
so De Silva is a natural fit for him.

00:19:31.860 --> 00:19:33.200
During marching drills one day,

00:19:33.200 --> 00:19:35.440
Andy is distracted when
he sees Colonel Cochrane,

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:37.930
no, not Conal Cochrane, Colonel Cochrane,

00:19:37.930 --> 00:19:39.750
carrying around a Good Guy doll outside.

00:19:39.750 --> 00:19:41.570
He doesn't have any proof
that it's Chucky yet,

00:19:41.570 --> 00:19:44.330
but it is a strange sight to
see at a military academy,

00:19:44.330 --> 00:19:46.470
and it causes him to drop
his rifle on the ground,

00:19:46.470 --> 00:19:48.370
which gets him in big
trouble with Shelton.

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:50.270
The trainees are drawn away not long after

00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:51.980
when they hear the
screams of a garbage man

00:19:51.980 --> 00:19:53.070
and run to go help him,

00:19:53.070 --> 00:19:55.300
only to find his lifeless
arm sticking out.

00:19:55.300 --> 00:19:57.000
That night, Whitehurst informs Barclay

00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:59.550
that he's gotta unpack, or
Shelton will be on him again.

00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:01.470
We saw the same thing
back at the foster home,

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:03.120
where Kyle had yet to unpack her things

00:20:03.120 --> 00:20:04.490
after three weeks of living there.

00:20:04.490 --> 00:20:07.000
This tells me that Andy has
also probably bounced around

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:08.560
to a lot of different homes over the years

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:10.190
and doesn't like getting
comfortable anywhere

00:20:10.190 --> 00:20:11.890
because he's moved around so much.

00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:14.130
Whitehurst also asks him
if he ever got a package,

00:20:14.130 --> 00:20:16.050
and he's confused at who
would be sending him one,

00:20:16.050 --> 00:20:17.740
and he puts up a picture
of him and his mom

00:20:17.740 --> 00:20:18.750
from when he was six.

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:19.730
These two things tell me

00:20:19.730 --> 00:20:21.890
that she's probably
still institutionalized;

00:20:21.890 --> 00:20:23.220
her life really got messed up

00:20:23.220 --> 00:20:25.080
by this whole ordeal more than anyone.

00:20:25.080 --> 00:20:26.850
Andy feels a sharp pain in his ankle

00:20:26.850 --> 00:20:29.370
and discovers Chucky hiding
under his bed with a knife.

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:32.210
He finds out that this time,
Chucky's just out for revenge.

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:34.050
Previously, Andy's life was protected

00:20:34.050 --> 00:20:35.470
because Chucky needed him alive

00:20:35.470 --> 00:20:36.890
to transfer his soul into him,

00:20:36.890 --> 00:20:38.760
but this time, Chucky
revealed his true nature

00:20:38.760 --> 00:20:40.560
to a younger cadet named Ronald Tyler

00:20:40.560 --> 00:20:41.740
before getting to Andy.

00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:43.870
As a result, Chucky can
only transfer himself

00:20:43.870 --> 00:20:44.710
into Tyler now.

00:20:44.710 --> 00:20:46.420
However, now being bigger and older,

00:20:46.420 --> 00:20:47.730
Andy's able to get the upper hand

00:20:47.730 --> 00:20:49.480
and start pounding Chucky into the ground,

00:20:49.480 --> 00:20:51.390
but that's when Shelton
hears the disturbance,

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:53.917
comes in and confiscates
the doll, and tells Andy.

00:20:53.917 --> 00:20:56.590
- You tell Whitehurst he's off the hook.

00:20:56.590 --> 00:20:58.200
I got myself another slave.

00:20:58.200 --> 00:20:59.670
- Once again, Andy's not gonna wait

00:20:59.670 --> 00:21:00.690
for Chucky to get to him,

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:02.910
so he sneaks out with a knife
while Shelton is asleep,

00:21:02.910 --> 00:21:04.750
but Chucky's appearance
causes him to flinch

00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:06.180
and wake Shelton up anyway.

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:08.610
We do see how Andy has matured
and gotten a bit smarter

00:21:08.610 --> 00:21:10.000
about what he lets out of his mouth,

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:11.690
because when Shelton asks
him what he's going on,

00:21:11.690 --> 00:21:12.770
he keeps it vague.

00:21:12.770 --> 00:21:13.870
- [ANDY] You wouldn't believe me.

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:16.040
- [ZAC] However, this gives
time for Chucky to scurry away,

00:21:16.040 --> 00:21:18.280
causing it to look like the
Good Guy doll had been stolen,

00:21:18.280 --> 00:21:20.930
and Shelton forces the
entire dorm to march outside,

00:21:20.930 --> 00:21:22.760
hoping to make an example of the thief.

00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:25.140
Andy is concerned that Chucky
is going to get to Tyler

00:21:25.140 --> 00:21:26.130
and possess his body,

00:21:26.130 --> 00:21:27.780
so he tries to bail out of the punishment,

00:21:27.780 --> 00:21:30.446
but Shelton catches him
and punches him in the gut.

00:21:30.446 --> 00:21:32.190
- [WRESTLING ANNOUNCER]
No way! This is awesome!

00:21:32.190 --> 00:21:33.780
- [ZAC] He's forced back
into the marching circle,

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:35.160
where his roommate Whitehurst asks him

00:21:35.160 --> 00:21:37.540
what he's trying to prove by
constantly pissing off Shelton.

00:21:37.540 --> 00:21:39.580
And after some prodding,
Andy tells him the truth

00:21:39.580 --> 00:21:41.710
about the doll being alive
and coming after Tyler.

00:21:41.710 --> 00:21:43.410
Like everybody else in Andy's life,

00:21:43.410 --> 00:21:44.820
Whitehurst doesn't believe him.

00:21:44.820 --> 00:21:46.480
That night, the Kent Academy students

00:21:46.480 --> 00:21:48.040
learn of the passing of Colonel Cochrane,

00:21:48.040 --> 00:21:49.210
and Andy can already assume

00:21:49.210 --> 00:21:50.870
that Chucky was involved in some way.

00:21:50.870 --> 00:21:52.340
The next morning, Andy is relieved

00:21:52.340 --> 00:21:53.700
to see that Tyler is okay,

00:21:53.700 --> 00:21:55.910
and he gets up during breakfast
to warn him about Chucky,

00:21:55.910 --> 00:21:57.380
but someone trips him on his way

00:21:57.380 --> 00:21:58.950
and the whole dining hall laughs at him,

00:21:58.950 --> 00:22:01.810
just highlighting how even
here, Barclay is an outcast.

00:22:01.810 --> 00:22:03.940
When he tries to convince
Tyler that Chucky is bad,

00:22:03.940 --> 00:22:06.330
he doesn't believe him, so
Andy gives him a pocket knife

00:22:06.330 --> 00:22:07.920
to hopefully protect himself with.

00:22:07.920 --> 00:22:09.200
His suspicions are heightened again

00:22:09.200 --> 00:22:11.660
when he notices Whitehurst
looking like he's seen a ghost,

00:22:11.660 --> 00:22:13.840
or in his case: a
children's doll possessed

00:22:13.840 --> 00:22:14.820
by a serial killer.

00:22:14.820 --> 00:22:16.130
This day would mark the beginning

00:22:16.130 --> 00:22:18.580
of Kent Military Academy's
annual war games,

00:22:18.580 --> 00:22:20.760
where the student body would
be split into two teams

00:22:20.760 --> 00:22:22.400
for a giant game of capture the flag

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:24.450
involving paintball guns
and camping in the woods

00:22:24.450 --> 00:22:25.750
to protect your team's flag.

00:22:25.750 --> 00:22:27.900
That evening, after Andy's
team has set up camp,

00:22:27.900 --> 00:22:29.700
they tell scary stories by the campfire,

00:22:29.700 --> 00:22:30.990
and Andy takes off on his own

00:22:30.990 --> 00:22:33.040
to try to stop Chucky
before he can get to Tyler,

00:22:33.040 --> 00:22:34.000
which is pretty selfless

00:22:34.000 --> 00:22:35.610
because Andy's probably gonna be safest

00:22:35.610 --> 00:22:36.700
staying right where we he his,

00:22:36.700 --> 00:22:39.130
surrounded by an army of
young soldiers in training.

00:22:39.130 --> 00:22:41.180
De Silva notices him
break off from the group

00:22:41.180 --> 00:22:43.310
and goes after him, and
she shows him an overlook

00:22:43.310 --> 00:22:45.410
where the two can see a
carnival off in the distance.

00:22:45.410 --> 00:22:47.590
Andy's response as they
share this moment together

00:22:47.590 --> 00:22:49.863
really shows how strange
his life has become.

00:22:52.490 --> 00:22:55.280
- [ANDY] Almost forgot
there are places like that.

00:22:55.280 --> 00:22:56.630
People just go to have fun.

00:22:58.010 --> 00:23:00.970
Listen. Somebody's out there.

00:23:00.970 --> 00:23:02.130
- It's a perfect example

00:23:02.130 --> 00:23:04.070
of why Barclay and De Silva work together.

00:23:04.070 --> 00:23:06.050
They're literally hiding
in the middle of nowhere,

00:23:06.050 --> 00:23:07.570
and he's concerned about Chucky,

00:23:07.570 --> 00:23:09.220
and she doesn't have a fear in the world.

00:23:09.220 --> 00:23:11.560
She kisses him, not the other way around.

00:23:11.560 --> 00:23:13.450
Alright! That's our boy!

00:23:13.450 --> 00:23:16.520
Our little cereal-spilling
brat is finally growing up.

00:23:16.520 --> 00:23:18.210
That same evening, he steals a map

00:23:18.210 --> 00:23:19.670
from cadet Lieutenant Shelton's tent

00:23:19.670 --> 00:23:20.720
and uses it to figure out

00:23:20.720 --> 00:23:22.220
where the red team might be hiding out

00:23:22.220 --> 00:23:23.580
so he can try to save Tyler.

00:23:23.580 --> 00:23:26.420
Whitehurst notices him leaving,
so Andy asks him to go with,

00:23:26.420 --> 00:23:29.520
but he won't budge, so as
always, Barclay's on his own.

00:23:29.520 --> 00:23:30.530
When he gets to red camp,

00:23:30.530 --> 00:23:32.410
another kid tells him
that Tyler went AWOL,

00:23:32.410 --> 00:23:34.850
or absent without leave,
with some guy named Charles.

00:23:34.850 --> 00:23:36.480
Eventually, he does find Tyler,

00:23:36.480 --> 00:23:38.280
and the rest of Andy's
unit catches up with him

00:23:38.280 --> 00:23:40.440
as they receive a strange
message over the radios,

00:23:40.440 --> 00:23:41.660
in which Chucky tells Barclay

00:23:41.660 --> 00:23:43.450
that he must bring the
kid up to the old Jeep,

00:23:43.450 --> 00:23:44.920
or there will be hell to pay.

00:23:44.920 --> 00:23:48.110
Andy realizes his catch-22
when he hears De Silva's voice

00:23:48.110 --> 00:23:50.040
in the background of
Chucky's transmission.

00:23:50.040 --> 00:23:51.630
As a group, they all go to the Jeep,

00:23:51.630 --> 00:23:53.440
and Shelton instructs Tyler and Barclay

00:23:53.440 --> 00:23:54.680
to go ahead and draw them out

00:23:54.680 --> 00:23:56.630
while the rest of the troops
circle around the area.

00:23:56.630 --> 00:23:58.470
They go ahead towards Chucky and Kristen,

00:23:58.470 --> 00:24:00.390
and the rest of the blue
team steps out of the trees

00:24:00.390 --> 00:24:02.810
and opens fire, but hits nothing.

00:24:02.810 --> 00:24:05.270
Seriously, not a single one
of them hits their target?

00:24:05.270 --> 00:24:07.120
I mean, what are they teaching
at this school anyway?

00:24:07.120 --> 00:24:09.230
I guess it doesn't make a huge
difference in the end though,

00:24:09.230 --> 00:24:11.150
because they're only
shooting paintball guns,

00:24:11.150 --> 00:24:12.950
and Chucky has been known to endure

00:24:12.950 --> 00:24:14.640
a few real bullets in the past.

00:24:14.640 --> 00:24:17.410
The red team, however, is
not using paintball guns.

00:24:17.410 --> 00:24:19.750
Chucky switched out their
ammo before the games began,

00:24:19.750 --> 00:24:21.770
so they're using real live ammunition.

00:24:21.770 --> 00:24:23.410
But since this is the first confrontation

00:24:23.410 --> 00:24:25.530
between the two teams,
they don't know it yet.

00:24:25.530 --> 00:24:27.150
So when they show up on the scene

00:24:27.150 --> 00:24:28.540
and open fire on their opponents,

00:24:28.540 --> 00:24:30.670
Lieutenant Shelton is shot and killed.

00:24:30.670 --> 00:24:32.040
Was Andy's first thought

00:24:32.040 --> 00:24:35.230
that he's not really gonna
miss Lieutenant Shelton?

00:24:35.230 --> 00:24:36.063
No comment.

00:24:36.063 --> 00:24:38.320
Shelton's second in command,
and presumed best friend,

00:24:38.320 --> 00:24:40.870
Major Ellis goes into a
rage and tackles Andy,

00:24:40.870 --> 00:24:42.310
assuming he was somehow responsible

00:24:42.310 --> 00:24:43.910
given his prior clashes with Shelton

00:24:43.910 --> 00:24:45.390
and general connection to any mischief

00:24:45.390 --> 00:24:46.580
going on since his arrival.

00:24:46.580 --> 00:24:48.200
All of this distraction allows Chucky

00:24:48.200 --> 00:24:49.630
to deliver yet another blow

00:24:49.630 --> 00:24:52.333
to Andy Barclay's already
reeling team of fighters.

00:25:04.829 --> 00:25:07.237
*crickets chirping*

00:25:08.630 --> 00:25:10.540
When Andy sees Tyler running after Chucky,

00:25:10.540 --> 00:25:13.540
he follows them, and Ms. De
Silva follows him for backup.

00:25:13.540 --> 00:25:14.560
They end up at the carnival,

00:25:14.560 --> 00:25:15.980
and go to the security tent to see

00:25:15.980 --> 00:25:17.530
if maybe someone had spotted Tyler,

00:25:17.530 --> 00:25:19.840
but upon their arrival, they
discover the security guard

00:25:19.840 --> 00:25:21.210
has already been taken out.

00:25:21.210 --> 00:25:23.050
Being the better shot,
De Silva takes the gun

00:25:23.050 --> 00:25:24.030
out of the guard's holster.

00:25:24.030 --> 00:25:25.680
Andy spots Chucky threatening Tyler

00:25:25.680 --> 00:25:27.280
as the two head into the employee entrance

00:25:27.280 --> 00:25:28.650
of the Devil's Lair dark ride,

00:25:28.650 --> 00:25:30.520
which, I mentioned this in
my Child's Play 3 episode

00:25:30.520 --> 00:25:33.100
of Things You Missed, but
this carnival ride is so cool.

00:25:33.100 --> 00:25:35.590
It's better than a lot of
actual permanent dark rides.

00:25:35.590 --> 00:25:37.500
I mean, it's certainly got Superstar Limo

00:25:37.500 --> 00:25:40.510
and Garfield's Nightmare beat,
and probably a lot of others.

00:25:40.510 --> 00:25:42.100
De Silva opens fire against Chucky,

00:25:42.100 --> 00:25:44.050
and he shoots back,
wounding her in the leg.

00:25:44.050 --> 00:25:46.470
Andy ties up her injury, and
she hands the gun off to him

00:25:46.470 --> 00:25:47.860
to continue on after Chucky.

00:25:47.860 --> 00:25:49.910
This is a significant
moment for his character.

00:25:49.910 --> 00:25:50.810
When Andy arrived,

00:25:50.810 --> 00:25:53.110
he was the helpless one
being protected by De Silva.

00:25:53.110 --> 00:25:55.520
Now, he has to use what she
taught him at the shooting range

00:25:55.520 --> 00:25:56.930
to protect her and Tyler.

00:25:56.930 --> 00:25:58.110
When Chucky begins the ritual,

00:25:58.110 --> 00:25:59.870
Andy remembers everything
that she taught him,

00:25:59.870 --> 00:26:01.390
and he's able to land a couple shots,

00:26:01.390 --> 00:26:03.000
first shooting off the doll's right arm,

00:26:03.000 --> 00:26:04.460
then landing one in the chest.

00:26:04.460 --> 00:26:06.497
When he goes to save
Tyler, Chucky jumps on him,

00:26:06.497 --> 00:26:08.590
and Tyler unintentionally
pays back the favor

00:26:08.590 --> 00:26:10.440
that Andy had done him by
trying to tell him the truth

00:26:10.440 --> 00:26:11.480
about Chucky earlier,

00:26:11.480 --> 00:26:12.830
by handing back the knife that Andy

00:26:12.830 --> 00:26:13.870
had originally given him.

00:26:13.870 --> 00:26:16.360
Using that, Barclay is able
to cut off Chucky's other hand

00:26:16.360 --> 00:26:18.260
and throw him into the
giant spinning fan blade,

00:26:18.260 --> 00:26:20.600
where he dies for the
third time, but notably,

00:26:20.600 --> 00:26:23.057
this is the first time he's
vanquished by Andy himself,

00:26:23.057 --> 00:26:24.910
and this third incarnation has sparked

00:26:24.910 --> 00:26:26.790
the most growth from Andy as a character.

00:26:26.790 --> 00:26:28.200
He gets Tyler back to safety

00:26:28.200 --> 00:26:29.850
and sees his girl, De Silva, off

00:26:29.850 --> 00:26:31.550
as she's carted out in an ambulance.

00:26:31.550 --> 00:26:33.840
Right after this, he's
arrested, though it's unclear

00:26:33.840 --> 00:26:35.310
if this was for the trespassing,

00:26:35.310 --> 00:26:37.570
or shooting a weapon in
public, or if he's being blamed

00:26:37.570 --> 00:26:39.210
for what happened to
Shelton and Whitehurst.

00:26:39.210 --> 00:26:40.990
At this point, it looks
like he's right back

00:26:40.990 --> 00:26:43.420
in the same scenario he's
been in two times before

00:26:43.420 --> 00:26:44.760
and he'll probably be kicked out

00:26:44.760 --> 00:26:47.470
and find himself on the road
to a new home once again.

00:26:47.470 --> 00:26:49.570
However, this time is
a little bit different,

00:26:49.570 --> 00:26:51.320
and Andy has himself to thank for it.

00:26:51.320 --> 00:26:52.830
Because instead of just crying Chucky

00:26:52.830 --> 00:26:55.190
like he had in the past and
expecting people to believe him,

00:26:55.190 --> 00:26:57.560
he focuses on trying to
take Chucky down himself,

00:26:57.560 --> 00:26:59.210
and this results in many other students

00:26:59.210 --> 00:27:01.380
discovering Chucky's
true nature on their own.

00:27:01.380 --> 00:27:02.960
I'm guessing because
so many people saw him

00:27:02.960 --> 00:27:05.260
with their own eyes, they were
able to back up his story,

00:27:05.260 --> 00:27:06.980
get him out of jail, and even prevent him

